I'm making this too convoluted. Let me simplify drastically: write a single `render_template` function that takes the template nodes, the data, the partial provider, and a helper closure. Let me rewrite hbs.rs cleanly.

Design:
```rust
pub struct Hbs<'a> {
    ctx: &'a RenderCtx,
    html: &'a HtmlConfig,
    index: Template,
    toc: Template,           // builtin toc.html template
    redirect: Template,
    head: Vec<Node>,
    header: Vec<Node>,
}

struct PageState<'a> {
    hbs: &'a Hbs<'a>,
    toc: String,      // the toc HTML for the {{toc}} helper
    previous: Option<String>,
    next: Option<String>,
}

impl PartialProvider for PageState { ... }  // head/header
impl Helpers for PageState { ... }          // resource, previous, next, toc
```
The `previous`/`next` helpers render their body with `link` in scope. To do that I need to render the body with a modified context. Since `Render` owns the stack, I can push a frame onto the stack before rendering the body. But `Render` is passed as `&mut Render` to the helper — so I can push/pop on it! 

```rust
"previous" => {
    if let Some(link) = &self.previous {
        // push a frame with link
        r.stack.push(Value::Object(vec![("link".to_string(), Value::Str(link.clone()))]));
        r.render_nodes(body);
        r.stack.pop();
    }
}
```
But `stack` is private in Render. Let me make it `pub` or add methods `push_frame`/`pop_frame`. Let me add public methods.

Let me rewrite hbs.rs cleanly now.

